{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2d5ed33ed3326fa1f189374f1712af495251c40c0e4a91394e3be81d744ba76c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_269be6fb1808de63d22842a5b3405f39b5df07f2069968c4444a31ead157f2d0","slc_b802a8812636b7f0bffd52f8d923c520704523ba01a333cdd7b22afd7c0c8e7a"],"source_ids":["src_03743a43d00a55f9bfaae00e25cbd01e"],"text":"App manifests use peerd.json with fields like kind, entry, agent (kind bound-app, profile, surface, name, instructions, runtime), and capabilities; a conforming Git repository places peerd.json and its entry file at the root.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_402c631786821379e914a8231aadfd4c38c1200a4aa4fc1c09a17bf031dacaf9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_78f3104cc068c268f2d50c8a768f0a8ca061ab3427d8e601f7d03627637d7010","slc_b6412a78f1b1bd06bdc909b42e722bdf5ca96adc04a7626d967d0b4b627322dc","slc_c9d778c826e00ca3a92b96a8d31bdc2e1a3573d6ebe60fee731adbbc3b5495cf","slc_eb30c6b0a3088f686027748fbcfa0b9dee595e86ea83d368d158d001589beb85"],"source_ids":["src_59e8ed91088259fd8c4792e06493c7c5"],"text":"Documented residual egress limits: Chrome DNR does not intercept worker-created WebSockets, private-network classification is lexical (no DNS resolution, so DNS rebinding is outside the check), and query strings/fragments are not a complete DLP boundary.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_47bd4b11d4833074141f3c11470f7d7ee0fefd90aa9243b3c9b4b295b36dedbb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2eecd92406520faeac19b0af9b9c3b41ea328f8414f4ea520d426a4d02c0649f","slc_7422341c4f1dba3ffa8cab6ba8270aca104ef86eec25c4f5a2f0a7b7061a252a","slc_78f3104cc068c268f2d50c8a768f0a8ca061ab3427d8e601f7d03627637d7010"],"source_ids":["src_59e8ed91088259fd8c4792e06493c7c5","src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"Credentials, network rules, confirmations, and audit stay with the extension; egress controls include refusal of private-network/cloud-metadata targets, denylist checks, and redirect blocking, with per-operation scoped network policies.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_493a5940a94099b8603b9a0fef44d07ade0064dd0ce5b00f2f566449ab05e48f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_072fec6e9eabd4547945dd6a76f98a5f082d13a6b5306b1717fe9dd53b006583","slc_719e92c45c7ed49351f3952bd5ece5386c6f64e8bf181f40d4754644f67705b9","slc_87804e2777493d58ff8b52e791db67905e5ca1e09b441d9ee4a3166630f740c5","slc_8b5ef7299478869f91a8e7c7dee13d16c98805f30f1c0f5f2d9ace5d0ba8375e","slc_f21e9fdb8448afaa1d3c6687c322097abbe20fa6eac47452434159141447eae8"],"source_ids":["src_03743a43d00a55f9bfaae00e25cbd01e"],"text":"Apps integrate via window.peerd APIs: agent.open() reveals a trusted drawer only during real user activation, agent.expose() declares observe/act semantic adapters, and peerd.data provides bounded JSON persistence (1 MB per write) mapped to data/<key>.json in the App's working tree.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_49c4ba9d289e2de2df1495b5d9705982d3b48fdc34cbca22dd730db9c4c20f70","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3d0b0de138be30e71044b19c2c5a31be2ce070f1ddf1547108971b81c6663589","slc_6efe583bdaf3ab33e4cbfc8449be22ecadd54696e0168703587c9331875fb075","slc_7097301b4d987d7f9f13ccd518fdf3ef30d80f325763096ee189828eb77cdeb2","slc_810ac08f3778795d2b69db4ce820986626e3be595e92a42e20e550d31288e5bd","slc_d04bdfbdd7266e346cea71771c5a2ff2617570726ef92d68247eeafaa676912e","slc_e14b9454232bfc157ee5299d151feb9b531875a3794ab73f65b02ec5bf068827"],"source_ids":["src_117164f539cc537ca3e038469252f654"],"text":"On Firefox, WebVM cannot boot from an extension page, threaded WebAssembly is unavailable, the Pod 'js' command is refused, Apps are disabled pending Firefox 154 adoption, offscreen-hosted tools are absent or degraded, and CDP-only automation features fall back to chrome.scripting.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6199c440af142e87948f652ed539e828ec4ee6ef42b59e5d5ae9f8a003ae860a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0418cc46a48b2aa94f99d28ac5dea21238f550aa7e8b44957ce8623d5308c738","slc_24f491124afe8ebfc2348bc5383d68ce856a38c86c6551e42ab4fb81db562b82","slc_8021139d614edba803682840f6bf1151e8759914e51c2751803bee9a8a52fef2","slc_bf4c3ff489ae02b4c2a1d181bb299ece8ae7ba071c23dbdfaad7a84c98e0c9c5"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"Repository development practice: development uses Bun commands (bun install, gen:dev, test, typecheck, lint, e2e:verify, preflight) across three test surfaces (Bun unit tests, in-browser Chrome/Gecko tests, live Chrome E2E), plus a red-team suite; generated files like extension/manifest.json must not be hand-edited and CI checks them for drift.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7ffb39d9dd53d3709f9ddb054d15da4cc24521bcb49841076596aff7ecbb9ea6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c8c64748de02c48cd36088f3f422287147dcca34560e0adbfac0807b63fe178","slc_a835bff28e62378118fdbfeb51f76c9fdcd3eb48a4644af23fe7e7419cccb204"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"The extension has five main modules, each exposing its public API via index.js: peerd-provider (model adapters), peerd-egress (vault, network policy, denylist, audit), peerd-engine (WebVM/Notebook/App/headless execution), peerd-runtime (agent loop, actors, tools, sessions, memory, permissions), and peerd-distributed (preview-only P2P).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_804ed06809a60749efeded84ac6a12179a8bf6c2a03d12e4c41016c38d8f8492","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5af5ef730b96e5f00bfd96aa6b2617132147c2b1a09276266f831ab18c53f285","slc_ce0ee46b8338227ff3193d165814d7b23e89e700ce5e972a0ea5da8be0895573","slc_e1fb681c1596d997113ba3dcca5aa7f79d7ab5bfdc7bba4e55c4f26f03ad2f00"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"Sessions, memory, skills, goals, review, and checkpoints live in the extension; a local vault holds secrets and protected security records, with passphrase unlock always available and passkey unlock dependent on WebAuthn PRF support.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_911ac392ddb6c1f71ea69f84caed15ac36739f8f5b786f40565c75f572a8bb36","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_57108e1f8376c4fb98caeb9013bd56547822349c3bb27beb5790a9a314bb32cf"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"The source extension is vanilla JavaScript with ES modules running directly when loaded unpacked, with no development bundler or transpiler; release packaging with Bun minifies only a disposable staging copy and preserves module boundaries and vendored bytes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9d436bff6373fd6860f6912f796530a39ac58b9820ec5f48b44e647f25d866eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4e5b0635080451e8433d776782bb5b5af8ddc6b8880d4b7967b809c65f2ab5f9"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"The shipped extension has no npm runtime dependencies; third-party runtime code is vendored under extension/vendor/ with SOURCE.txt provenance files and SHA-256 pinning in vendor.lock.json, verified by bun run check:vendor.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b0e0b7e93437fe7741ab03b85ed11bba215278617b02b76b74ea6b49c13ec04b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f5cbff8369f35e17a42aa7163c39f0404090956ba3e66675be7cee2f8048516f"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"peerd is described as a general-purpose agent runtime built on browser primitives (Workers, origins, sandboxing, OPFS, WASM/WASI, WebRTC, WebAuthn, WebExtensions) that runs inside Chrome and Firefox.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_daf7653b96fb12bd81fdb2e05601b573c5f9449df6538c91823d10b66c9978e0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"notasithlord/peerd@12d1a54976bc snapshot c54f3ca7139dac7c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_76dd2e96cac99dd83e70879e638f95d4f863e5993aa439671da1179e5e76747a","slc_e1fb681c1596d997113ba3dcca5aa7f79d7ab5bfdc7bba4e55c4f26f03ad2f00"],"source_ids":["src_fff4f1b8fce156b9ae5b28baa4870253"],"text":"The main agent delegates page and compute-environment work to separate keyless actors whose tools are scoped to that environment; non-orchestrator agent loops run in dedicated worker heaps, and requests fail if the browser cannot prove that boundary.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_23953f901a384964a25ec63d753351ac"}
